  <diagram name="10 Video Generation" id="10_Video_Generation">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2200" pageHeight="1400" math="0" shadow="0" background="#0b0f14">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="10_Video_Generation_title" value="Video Generation — composite B/W signal" style="text;html=1;fontSize=18;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#e6edf3;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="24" width="520" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10_Video_Generation_note_1" value="F2b (7425) ORs the two paddles, the net, and the ball into the white video; the SCORE signal is mixed through a higher 1.2K resistor so it appears dimmer. A resistor summing network + 5µF coupling cap form a 4-level DAC (sync/black/gray/white). Most gates here are halves of packages drawn on other sheets (F2,G1,E4,A4,G3,B2) — carried by named nets." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#8b949e;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="56" width="980" height="84" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10_Video_Generation_note_2" value="F2b (the 7425 home package is on sheet 07 Score) ORs the two paddles, the net and the ball; its output arrives here as named net f2b_o and feeds the 2.2K video resistor." style="text;html=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#8b949e;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="130" width="980" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="10_Video_Generation_Rsync_stub" value="Rsync sync 1K" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#161b22;strokeColor=#d29922;fontColor=#f0d68a;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;arcSize=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
